--TEST--
`Core\Process::run` takes `array<string>` for its arguments, so an argument list holding a `tainted string` does not compile, the same as a tainted path — `rule:core-classes/process-is-argv-only`, `rule:security/process-exec-capability`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// An environment value is `tainted`, and the argument list is the slot under
// test: the path is a literal. The argument element has no qualifier of its
// own, and `array<tainted string>` is not `array<string>`, so the ordinary
// argument check is what refuses it. No grant is written, and none is reached.
var $name = Core\Env::get("NAME") ?? "x";
var $result = Core\Process::run("/bin/echo", [$name]);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `string|tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:7:47
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
